etitive we'll also have  Lyft co-founder John Zimmer being  interviewed we have reported that Lyft  has slowed hiring along with many many  other tech companies and Lyft has spent  very carefully on driver incentives in  the midst of a driver short Edge so John  will be talking about that as well as  live self-driving car strategy and also  some more Mobility initiatives like  bikes scooters and car rentals we also  have snap CEO Evan Spiegel who will be  talking about the company's augmented  reality focus and how he's been  navigating the turbulent economic  climate this is another company that has  had to lay off some employees recently  and just re-prioritize things their  Shares are down quite significantly now  and you know as you can see the economy  and how entrepreneurs are weathering the  storm is a really Common Thread at this  year's Tech live now our guests include  more than just company Executives who  else can we expect to hear from yeah  that's right and I'm actually really  excited about this for one digital  artist people is joining us on stage his  real name is Mike winkelmann he sold a  piece of digital artwork for 69.3  million dollars in a Christie's Auction  that was a record-breaking sale and he's  really just ushered in a new way of  thinking about the value of digital art  and nfts we also have Ben McKenzie  joining us he is an actor probably best  known for his leading role in the OC he  spent much of the pandemic learning  about cryptocurrencies and he's been an  incredibly outspoken crypto skeptic  which which is a little bit ironic  considering how many celebrities have  touted cryptocurrencies and nfts in  recent months we also have Hayley Bieber  joining us she is a model and  entrepreneur and Haley is an example of  somebody who's really just harnessing  the power of social media e-commerce and  streaming to create a brand the Creator  economy is of course booming so her  business strategies will be a really  interesting one to watch we will also  have Tariq Trotter on the lineup he is a  Grammy winner and perhaps most well  known as being the front man and  co-founder of the hip-hop band The Roots  he's now also a venture capitalist and  he plans to invest in underrepresented  entrepreneurs so you mentioned some of  the topics our guests are going to talk  about but what are some of the big  interesting themes that will be covered  in this year's event that jump out to  you yeah so the economy jobs and layoffs  that is going to be a major major thread  throughout the entire event crypto and  nfts that's also going to be a pretty  big Focus the metaverse everyone's  talking about it the journal has covered  it extensively in podcasts and Reporting  we are definitely going to be talking  about that and the potential for the  business use case for the metaverse but  also the critical aspect of it we also  can't forget that Tech live is happening  the same week of the Elon Musk Twitter  deal which is as of now at least  expected to close soon  you know one of the things that a lot of  people always talk about when it comes  to Big Tech and especially in recent  years is about regulation what can we  expect to hear on that front  yeah so lawmakers have been cracking  down on big Tech and they have been  scrutinizing many aspects of Technology  including cryptocurrencies for example  and also social media so there's going  to be quite a bit of talk about that Pat  gelsinger as I mentioned will be talking  about the chips act which is one of the  you know most significant pieces of  legislation that was passed recently in  the tech sector and you know U.S China  competition is going to be a pretty big  Focus as well there's been a lot of talk  about how the US can bolster Innovation  and compete against China so that will  be a pretty big Focus all right that was  wsj's live journalism news editor Sarah  Castellanos Sarah thank you again for  joining us today thank you  and that's it for today's Tech news  briefing Tech live begins today Monday  at 11 30 a.m Pacific we'll have live  coverage of the event on our website  wsj.com and if you're a Wall Street  Journal subscriber you can head to  wsj.com Tech live for a complimentary  online pass I'm Julie Chang for the Wall  Street Journal thanks for listening  [Music]  [Music]

